  "summary": "This study compares three Ti3C2Tx electrodes: HF-etched Ti3C2Tx, LiCl-KCl molten-salt-treated M-Ti3C2Tx, and LiCl-KCl-K2CO3 molten-salt-treated KM-Ti3C2Tx. The molten-salt carbonate treatment introduces potassium oxygenated-complex intercalation, increases O termination content, and expands the layer spacing to 1.05\u20131.21 nm. KM-Ti3C2Tx is the headline and best-performing electrode, reaching 340 F g\u22121 at 0.5 A g\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4; the abstract/conclusion additionally report 323.6 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121. Electrode thickness, flake size, BET surface area, pore diameter, porosity, tortuosity, and volumetric/areal capacitances were not reported."
